A||||2||Mach10||Intermittent engine problems||||5||
Z||000000||Mach10||07-05-2001||07:53 PM||||This one has me stumped. Gas mileage is good: about 290-300 km city per tank, power is fine, but every now and then the cars an absolute BASTARD to start, and idles funny, dogs, and misses. Give it some gas, and it behaves perfectly. No codes, no other obvious issues, just the occasional hard start, and crappy idle. I'm thinking my coil's on it's way out, since I've done plugs, wires, 02, EGR, and reset codes. This HAS to be electrical, given the intermittency... [/confused]<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||07-05-2001||08:41 PM||||Do yo have the means to check the throttle position sensor?  Either a scanner or manually with a multi-meter?  If the TPS is telling the computer you're giving it gas (but you're not), it will not pulse the injectors correctly but once you do really give it gas it will run better.  Make sure you don't press the accellerator while turning on the key as the computer takes the initial reading then.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-05-2001||08:51 PM||||That's a good point. Out of habit (old car) I'd always tap the gas while starting it if it gives me trouble. That might be the root of my idle problems. <BR>I'm going to see if the hard-starting is linked to the rough idle issue... If they're separate, then I'm thinking bad coil, although I have no problems after it's running.||||reg||14
